+# Retention planning: summary
+
+## What changed
+
+- `vaultsnap/retention.py`: implemented `plan_retention(snapshots, policy, now)`. It plans only and deletes nothing. `Plan` and the signature are unchanged.
+- `tests/test_retention_adr.py` (new): 17 tests for the ADR rules that the existing tests do not cover. `tests/test_retention.py` is unchanged.
+- `SUMMARY.md`: this file.
+
+## Which ADR governs which part
+
+- **Core model, inputs, ordering, output, set-aside rules, keep_last, the bucket rule, independence of rules, empty policy:** ADR-0001. Ordering is by `taken_at`, with ties broken by the greater id. Bucket rules keep the newest snapshot of each of the N newest non-empty buckets. Empty periods do not use up N.
+- **Weekly buckets:** ADR-0003 (supersedes the "Weeks" section of ADR-0001). Weeks are ISO weeks, keyed `(iso_year, iso_week)`, Monday start. Monthly and yearly keys still use the calendar year and month.
+- **Day boundaries:** ADR-0004 (supersedes ADR-0002, which was UTC-only). The bucket date is `taken_at` converted to `tz_offset_minutes`, minus `day_start_hour` hours, then taking the date. All daily, weekly, monthly and yearly keys come from that date. Ordering, `keep_last` and the `now` comparison use the real instant.
+- ADR-0002 is retired and not applied.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+- A naive `now`, a naive `taken_at`, or a duplicate id raises `ValueError`.
+- Snapshots with a `protect_tags` tag, or with `taken_at > now`, are set aside. They are always kept, do not count toward any N, and are never a bucket representative. A snapshot at exactly `now` is not set aside.
+- If all five rules are off, everything is kept.
+- `keep` and `prune` are lists of ids, each newest first.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `python -m unittest -v` (Python 3.14.3, run in the repo root): **24 tests, all OK.**
+  - Before the change, the 7 tests in `tests/test_retention.py` all errored with `NotImplementedError`.
+  - After the change, those 7 pass unmodified, and the 17 new tests pass.
+- The expected values in the new tests were worked out by hand from the ADRs. The ISO test was checked against the Sunday-start result to confirm it tells the two apart, but I did not run a mutation check of the code.
+
+## Not verified / open points
+
+- Only Python 3.14.3 was tested. The code uses only long-standing stdlib features (`timezone`, `timedelta`, `date.isocalendar()` indexed as a tuple), so I expect it to work on other 3.x versions, but I have not confirmed that.
+- The rules are implemented as written. No real snapshot data was run through the planner.
+- The nightly job is not checked end to end. Nothing deletes snapshots yet, which matches the task.
+
+## Things outside the allowed files (not changed)
+
+- `README.md`: the retention section is labelled as an old draft and says the ADRs win. It still describes Sunday weeks and UTC days, which the ADRs replace. Consider rewriting or removing that section so readers are not misled.
+- `CHANGELOG.md`: says "Retention pruning is being added". That is still accurate, but once it ships the entry should be updated.
+- `docs/adr/0002-bucket-timezone.md` is superseded and is left as is, as the ADRs record it.
